            "TimesLTStd-Roman"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            5.02,
            7.0,
            7.03,
            10.0
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "of the Laplacian on the discrete torus is a finite determinant, in the sense of linear algebra.",
          "bbox": [
            96.38,
            259.64,
            468.42,
            269.64
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "TimesLTStd-Roman"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            10.0
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "However, the determinant of the Laplacian on the continuous torus is obtained through zeta",
          "bbox": [
            96.38,
            271.64,
            468.42,
            281.64
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "TimesLTStd-Roman"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            10.0
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "regularization, which adds an entirely new level of complexity to the matter.",
          "bbox": [
            96.38,
            283.64,
            400.66,
            293.64
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "TimesLTStd-Roman"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            10.0
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Let us briefly explain how the discrete Gaussian comes into play in this setting. Following",
          "bbox": [
            108.33,
            295.64,
            468.43,
            305.64
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "TimesLTStd-Roman"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            10.0
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "the usual formalism, logdet∆Zd/AnZd is related to the Mellin transform of the trace of the heat",
          "bbox": [
            96.38,
            306.66,
            468.42,
            319.05
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMMI7",
            "CMR10",
            "MSBM7",
            "TimesLTStd-Italic",
            "TimesLTStd-Roman"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            5.02,
            7.0,
            7.03,
            10.0
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "kernel. The trace of the heat kernel is the theta function, which in our discrete setting involves",
          "bbox": [
            96.38,
            319.64,
            468.43,
            329.64
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "TimesLTStd-Roman"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            10.0
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "dQ",
          "bbox": [
            257.96,
            329.45,
            267.4,
            339.45
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMEX10",
            "TimesLTStd-Italic"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            7.03,
            10.0
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "e−2tInjkj(2t). A careful analysis of the asymptotics",
          "bbox": [
            270.06,
            335.72,
            468.42,
            349.04
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMR10",
            "CMSY7",
